GOLDMAN Sacs on Urban Co : Neutral, TP Rs 130

Analyst day  key takeaways
(i) UC could continue to grow NTV higher than its guided 20%+ in the core business, with even stronger visibility on margins;
(ii) Core business moats continue to get stronger, with improving densification and partner utilisation driving accelerating user growth;
(iii) Foray into Air Conditioners is unlikely to be material to capex or alter Native's margin trajectory;
(iv) A large part of InstaHelp investment is towards market build-out, which will drop off in a few quarters, helping UC reduce losses in the segment even if competition stays elevated, per the company;
(v) Announced capital raise is likely to be deployed either towards M&A or to keep buffer if Instahelp competition becomes more intense, but UC is unlikely to enter new product categories or geographies

MS on Urban Co ; OW, TP Rs 190

Analyst day takeaways

a) improvement in growth in India consumer services NTV ex Instahelp is structural;
b) reiterated outlook of 3QF28 breakeven and Rs10bn F31 at consolidated adj EBITDA level;
c) balance sheet is already strong so fund-raising is for strategic flexibility.
